  "salt": "THcz1JW3B4dHAUKUyU3ziQ==",
  "text": "Fairy food is a folkloric motif. Tales say fairy fare tasted better than any meal on earth. Yet the fairy folk prized the plainer meals of mortals. They slipped into our world to steal them. Butter drew them most of all. They took away its inner essence, the foyson. For all its flavor, fairy food gave the body little strength. Many charms kept butter safe. People put mullein leaves or holy water into the churn. Newly baked bread also drew the fairies. They carried it off when nobody watched. At other times the fairies gave food from their own stores. They helped human neighbors in lean times. Stories of Ireland's Great Hunger of the 1840s tell of gifts of sweets.",
